> This moves platforms inside the scene setup

~~No it doesn't – it happens _before_ scene setup, after `register_scene_singletons()`.~~ Arguably they all should be registered earlier – before/during initialization level core :thinking:.

(EDIT: My bad - scene initialization doesn't start with `OS::get_singleton()->benchmark_begin_measure("Scene", "Modules and Extensions");` but earlier)

> what documentation are you referring to

According to Godot docs classes such as `JavaClass`, `JavaClassWrapper`, and `JavaObject` should be available and mocked in non-platform builds (and they are doing so – they are just available after extension has been initialized):

For example:

https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_javaobject.html
> Note: This class only works  on Android. On any other platform, this class does nothing.

https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_javaclasswrapper.html#class-javaclasswrapper-method-get-exception
> Note: This method  only works on Android. On every other platform, this method will always return null.

https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_javaclasswrapper.html#class-javaclasswrapper-method-wrap
> Note: This method only works on Android. On every other platform, this method does nothing and returns an empty [JavaClass](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_javaclass.html#class-javaclass).


